<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="036" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Self-service submitter authz (Tier-2 requester==caller) + app-only SPE upload</title>
    <phase>P3 Legal Front Door intake MVP</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:030,031</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth-sensitive Tier-2 record-scope predicate + app-only SPE upload on the shared external-access surface; the NFR-08 per-module negative test lives here; tags bff-api/auth — FULL per CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-critical: the requester==caller Tier-2 predicate + app-only (no OBO) SPE upload with authz-before-stream — a single scoping omission is a cross-user data leak; brownfield re-host of an OBO upload path.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Auth-sensitive; hardens the shared Front Door BFF group (031) + SPE surface; must not race another BFF editor (conflict-check with teams-app-r1).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030,031</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Harden the Front Door module (031 group) with FR-17 self-service submitter authz: a Tier-2 record-scope predicate requester==caller so a Front Door user can create and see ONLY their own sprk_servicerequests, plus app-only SPE upload of submitted documents via SpeFileStore (ADR-007) — no OBO, keyed on documentId, authz-before-stream. Resolve the caller via CallerPrincipalResolver + lazily attribute the requester Contact by oid; enforce requester==caller on read AND write server-side. This is one instance of the NFR-08 per-module record-scope mechanism.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Broker-only external auth (ADR-028 +A1/A3, no OBO), per-endpoint/route-group authz filters (ADR-008), SPE via SpeFileStore app-only + authz-before-stream (ADR-007), ProblemDetails (ADR-019).</role>
  <goal>The Front Door group enforces requester==caller: a GET my-requests returns only the caller's own sprk_servicerequests, a GET by-id for someone else's request returns 403/404 (no data), and a submit attributes the requester to the caller's Contact (lazily resolved-or-created by oid). Document upload streams app-only via SpeFileStore (keyed on documentId, no OBO, no Graph pointer exposure), with authz enforced BEFORE any bytes stream (an unauthorized upload returns 403 with no bytes written). This is the NFR-08 record-scope mechanism instance for the Front Door module.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-17 (spec.md line 67): a Front Door user (workforce SSO) can create and see ONLY their own requests (Tier-2 predicate requester==caller, one instance of the per-module record-scope mechanism in NFR-08); document upload streams app-only via the SPE broker (no OBO, no pointer exposure). 031 established the Front Door group + submit/status and explicitly left the requester==caller enforcement + app-only upload as the "034 hardening seam" (now this task, 036). 030 supplies the sprk_requester Contact lookup + the submitted-document linkage. The caller is resolved plane-agnostically via CallerPrincipalResolver (delivered by teams-app-r1); internal workforce users are attributed via a lazily-created Contact bound by oid (FR-11; 023 built the resolve-or-create — reuse it). Tier-1 (module entitlement) is separate + already enforced by the group filter; Tier-2 (record scope) is THIS task. NFR-08 requires a negative Tier-2 test per module.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md (FR-17 line 67; NFR-08 two-tier model + per-module negative test)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/tasks/031-typed-intake-framework.poml (the MapFrontDoorEndpoints group + submit/status this task hardens; the "hardening seam" marker)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs (plane-agnostic caller; CallerPrincipal :66 — resolve the caller identity)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter.cs (group-level Tier-1 filter — Tier-2 is added at the handler/service layer)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/**/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs (ComposeAsync — the workforce record-scope predicate pattern to follow for requester==caller)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**/InviteExternalUserEndpoint.ResolveOrCreateContactAsync (:172) + ExternalParticipationService (resolve :231) (lazy Contact-by-oid attribution to reuse; 023 wired this)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/**/SpeFileStore.cs (app-only upload/download; ADR-007; key on documentId; authz-before-stream)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md, .claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md, .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>030 (sprk_requester Contact lookup + submitted-document linkage) + 031 (Front Door group + submit/status) must be complete. 023 (lazy Contact attribution resolve-or-create by oid) is reused for requester attribution. 037 (my-requests UI + feedback) renders the requester==caller reads this task enforces.</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Broker-only: the upload + the requester==caller reads run app-only downstream (SPE + Dataverse) — the caller token authenticates ONLY to the BFF and is NEVER exchanged for an OBO token. No OBO on any path in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">All SPE uploads/downloads go through SpeFileStore app-only; key on documentId; authz-before-stream (enforce requester==caller / entitlement BEFORE any bytes stream); never expose a Graph drive/item pointer to the client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Tier-2 requester==caller MUST be enforced SERVER-SIDE on BOTH read (list + by-id) AND write (submit/upload) — never rely on the client to scope. The requester is the caller's Contact, resolved-or-created lazily by oid (reuse 023). Tier-1 (module entitlement) stays on the group filter; do NOT conflate the two tiers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Tier-2 enforcement is at the handler/service layer within the existing Front Door route-group (no new global middleware); errors via ProblemDetails (ADR-019).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF addition: state the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); run dotnet publish -c Release and report compressed size + delta vs baseline 46.90 MB incl PDBs (ceiling ≤60 MB); run /conflict-check before the BFF PR (teams-app-r1 shares Api/ExternalAccess/** + Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
