    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Record-scope predicate" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/**/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs">Follow ComposeAsync's server-side record-scope predicate shape for requester==caller (Tier-2), keyed on the resolved caller.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Lazy Contact by oid" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**/ExternalParticipationService.cs:231">Resolve-or-create the requester Contact by oid (reuse 023) — do not require a licensed systemuser.</pattern>
      <pattern name="App-only SPE" location=".claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md">Upload/download via SpeFileStore app-only; authz-before-stream; key on documentId; no Graph pointer to the client.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load spec.md FR-17 (line 67) + NFR-08 + ADR-028/007/008 + bff-extensions.md + the 031 group (the hardening-seam markers). Read AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeAsync + ExternalParticipationService (lazy Contact-by-oid) + SpeFileStore. Run /conflict-check for the external-access BFF surface.</step>
    <step order="2">Requester attribution: on submit, resolve the caller via CallerPrincipalResolver + resolve-or-create the requester Contact by oid (reuse 023). Set sprk_requester (030) to that Contact. App-only.</step>
    <step order="3">Tier-2 read enforcement: add a requester==caller predicate (following ComposeAsync) to the Front Door reads — GET my-requests returns only the caller's requests; GET by-id returns 403/404 for another caller's request (no data). Server-side, at the handler/service layer within the group.</step>
    <step order="4">App-only SPE upload: implement submitted-document upload via SpeFileStore app-only, keyed on documentId (link to the 030 submitted-document linkage), with authz-before-stream — verify entitlement + requester==caller BEFORE any bytes stream; an unauthorized upload returns 403 with no bytes written; never expose a Graph pointer.</step>
    <step order="5">Cache: if my-requests/participation reads are Redis-cached, ensure invalidation on submit (ADR-009) so a new request appears for its owner immediately.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: KEEP-path integration tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ — user A cannot see user B's requests (list + by-id, the NFR-08 negative), an unauthorized upload returns 403 with no bytes, requester is attributed to the caller Contact, and no OBO token is acquired (app-only assertion). NO Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; / DI-registration / ctor-null tests (ADR-038).</step>
    <step order="7">Build: dotnet publish -c Release — report compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB. State the Placement Justification in the task notes / PR body.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the app-only SPE upload or the requester==caller read cannot be satisfied without OBO — i.e. any reused component (SpeFileStore upload path, Dataverse read, or Contact attribution) requires an OBO/user token with no app-only variant — STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required (ADR-028/NFR-01: no OBO on any SPA path). Do NOT introduce OBO to make the upload/read work. Present the component + the app-only gap + options.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell, /conflict-check</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Not required for this task (client my-requests UI is 037)</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/** — Tier-2 requester==caller predicate on the Front Door reads (list + by-id) + requester Contact attribution on submit</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/** — app-only SpeFileStore submitted-document upload (documentId-keyed, authz-before-stream)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/** — NFR-08 negative (A cannot see B), unauthorized-upload-403-no-bytes, requester-attribution, no-OBO KEEP-path integration tests</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given user A's requests, when user A calls GET my-requests, then only A's own sprk_servicerequests are returned (Tier-2 requester==caller).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (NFR-08): given a request owned by user B, when user A calls GET by-id for it, then the server returns 403/404 with NO record data — A never sees B's request.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a submit, when the caller is resolved, then sprk_requester is attributed to the caller's Contact (lazily resolved-or-created by oid) — not a licensed systemuser.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a document upload, when it streams, then it goes through SpeFileStore app-only keyed on documentId with NO OBO and NO Graph pointer exposed to the client.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (authz-before-stream): given an unauthorized upload (caller lacks entitlement or requester!=caller), when attempted, then the server returns 403 and NO bytes are written to SPE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the reads + upload, when reviewed, then no OBO/user token is acquired downstream (app-only assertion in tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the BFF build, when dotnet publish -c Release runs, then compressed size is reported with delta vs 46.90 MB and is ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Spec FR-17 (line 67) + NFR-08. This task completes the 031 hardening seam (requester==caller Tier-2 + app-only upload). Reuse AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeAsync (predicate shape), 023's lazy Contact-by-oid, and SpeFileStore app-only. Tier-1 module entitlement stays on the group filter; Tier-2 record scope is here. 037 renders the my-requests reads this task enforces. §10 BFF: Placement Justification + publish size + conflict-check mandatory. No OBO on any path (ADR-028/A3).</notes>
